---
/**
 * Frequently asked questions. Every answer restates the README (Install,
 * Requirements, Lossless, Privacy, "Why Stash isn't on the Play Store",
 * "When background sync stops working"); keep them in step when it changes.
 *
 * Each answer has an id (faq-*) so other pages can link straight to it;
 * browsers open the question when its answer is linked.
 */
import Icon from '../Icon.astro';
import { LINKS } from '../../data/site';
---

<section class="section faq" id="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
  <div class="container layout">
    <div class="intro">
      <p class="overline">FAQ</p>
      <h2 id="faq-title" class="section-title">Questions, answered</h2>
      <p class="section-intro">Didn't find yours? The Discord is the place to ask, and answers come fast.</p>
      <a class="button button-secondary ask" href={LINKS.discord}>
        <Icon name="discord" size="20px" />
        Ask on Discord
      </a>
    </div>

    <div class="list">
      <details>
        <summary>Is Stash free?<Icon name="chevron-down" class="chevron" /></summary>
        <div class="answer" id="faq-free">
          <p>
            Yes. Stash is free and open source under the GPL-3.0, with no ads, no subscription and no Stash
            account. To sync a library you need your own Spotify and/or YouTube Music account.
          </p>
          <p>If Stash replaced a subscription for you, you can <a href="#community">support the project</a>.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Why isn't Stash on the Play Store?<Icon name="chevron-down" class="chevron" /></summary>
        <div class="answer" id="faq-play-store">
          <p>
            Stash downloads audio from YouTube and Spotify, which violates both services' Terms of Service, and
            Google Play policy bans apps that facilitate unauthorized downloads. Every project in this space,
            like NewPipe, YTDLnis, SpotTube and InnerTune, is distributed outside the Play Store for the same
            reason.
          </p>
          <p>
            That isn't a workaround. It's a principled choice: open-source tools that give users control over
            their own libraries don't belong in a gatekept store that could revoke them on a whim. GitHub
            Releases is the right home for Stash.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>How do I install it?<Icon name="chevron-down" class="chevron" /></summary>
        <div class="answer" id="faq-install">
          <p>
            On your phone, open the <a href={LINKS.download}>latest release</a> and download the
            <code>Stash-v*.apk</code> file. Open it, and if Android warns about installs from unknown sources,
            allow them for your browser and try again. Then tap Install.
          </p>
          <p>
            Stash checks GitHub for new releases and lets you know when one is out. To get updates through
            <a href={LINKS.obtainium}>Obtainium</a>, add <code>https://github.com/rawnaldclark/Stash</code> to it.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Where does lossless come from?<Icon name="chevron-down" class="chevron" /></summary>
        <div class="answer" id="faq-lossless">
          <p>
            Stash ships no shared user accounts: there's no bundled Qobuz account and no shared token pool. FLAC
            comes from a source you pick:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <strong>Your own Qobuz account</strong>, connected in Settings › Audio &amp; Quality. Your email
              and password are sent once to Qobuz to mint a token; Stash keeps the token, not the password.
            </li>
            <li><strong>Your own relay endpoint</strong>, if you run one.</li>
            <li>
              <strong>Stash's own relay</strong>, in the official release build only: a relay the project runs on
              a few paid Qobuz accounts. It's sized as a bridge, not a main path, and your phone stops using it
              once you connect your own account.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            When no lossless source can serve a song, playback and downloads fall back to AAC or Opus, and Home
            tells you so instead of pretending.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Is my data safe?<Icon name="chevron-down" class="chevron" /></summary>
        <div class="answer" id="faq-privacy">
          <p>
            Stash has no account server, no analytics and no third-party crash reporters. Your credentials live on
            your phone, with the Spotify, YouTube and Discord tokens encrypted (AES-256-GCM, via Google's
            <a href={LINKS.tink}>Tink</a>), and each one is only ever sent back to the service it came from. No
            host the project runs ever sees one.
          </p>
          <p>
            Lyrics, scrobbling, artist info and lossless have hosts of their own. The
            <a href="/privacy">privacy page</a> lists everything Stash can reach, and what each one is sent. Found
            a security issue? Please <a href={LINKS.security}>report it privately</a>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>What do I need?<Icon name="chevron-down" class="chevron" /></summary>
        <div class="answer" id="faq-requirements">
          <p>
            A phone running Android 8.0 or later, and a Spotify and/or YouTube Music account. Offline mode needs
            room for your music: about 9–15 GB for a medium library, depending on how much you sync. Online mode
            needs almost nothing.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Sync stops in the background. What can I do?<Icon name="chevron-down" class="chevron" /></summary>
        <div class="answer" id="faq-background-sync">
          <p>
            Some phones, especially from Samsung, Xiaomi, OnePlus and Huawei, close background apps aggressively
            to save battery. If a sync fails partway with a foreground-service error, open your phone's Settings ›
            Apps › Stash › Battery and set it to Unrestricted. You only need to do this once.
          </p>
          <p>
            If that's not enough on your phone, <a href={LINKS.dontKillMyApp}>dontkillmyapp.com</a> has steps for
            each manufacturer.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .layout {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 5fr) minmax(0, 7fr);
    gap: clamp(40px, 6vw, 96px);
    align-items: start;
  }

  .intro {
    position: sticky;
    top: 112px;
  }

  .ask {
    margin-top: 28px;
  }

  .list {
    display: grid;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  details {
    border-radius: var(--radius-xl);
    border: 1px solid var(--glass-border);
    background: var(--glass);
    transition:
      background-color 200ms ease,
      border-color 200ms ease;
  }

  details:hover,
  details[open] {
    border-color: var(--glass-border-bright);
  }

  details[open] {
    background: var(--glass-hover);
  }

  summary {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 16px;
    padding: 20px 22px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-xl);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(1.0625rem, 1rem + 0.3vw, 1.25rem);
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.3;
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
  }

  summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }

  summary :global(.chevron) {
    color: var(--text-2);
    transition: transform 200ms ease;
  }

  details[open] summary :global(.chevron) {
    transform: rotate(180deg);
  }

  .answer {
    display: grid;
    gap: 12px;
    padding: 0 22px 22px;
    color: var(--text-2);
    scroll-margin-top: 160px;
  }

  .answer ul {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    padding-left: 1.2em;
  }

  .answer li::marker {
    color: var(--purple);
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .layout {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }

    .intro {
      position: static;
    }
  }
</style>
